  "id": "basilar-membrane",
  "term": "basilar membrane",
  "definition": "The basilar membrane is a membrane in the cochlea that supports the hair cells of the organ of Corti. When sound-driven fluid moves in the cochlea, this membrane is displaced, helping stimulate the hair cells so mechanical sound vibrations are converted into neural activity.",
